{%- comment -%}
  sie-redirect — the Shopify storefront is not the store. sie.market is.

  Checkout's logo ("Navigate to Online Store") links to the shop's root, its
  cart icon to /cart, the order page's "Continue shopping" and the
  notification emails' "visit our store" to the root again. All of those
  land on this theme, which showed a second, unbranded sie. Every page this
  theme would draw now sends the visitor to https://sie.market/ instead.

  Left alone, because Shopify needs them or a shopper might:
    - the theme editor and its previews        (design_mode / visual_preview_mode)
    - /policies/*                              (checkout links its policies here)
    - the password and captcha pages
    - customer account pages                   (customers/*)
  Checkout itself, /cart/<variant>:<qty> permalinks, /checkouts and order
  status pages are not drawn by the theme at all, so this never touches them.

  Rendered first thing in <head> of layout/theme.liquid:
    {% render 'sie-redirect' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sie_keep = false
  if request.design_mode or request.visual_preview_mode
    assign sie_keep = true
  endif
  case request.page_type
    when 'policy', 'password', 'captcha'
      assign sie_keep = true
  endcase
  if request.page_type contains 'customers/'
    assign sie_keep = true
  endif
-%}
{%- unless sie_keep -%}
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=https://sie.market/">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://sie.market/">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <script>location.replace('https://sie.market/');</script>
{%- endunless -%}
